index="botsv1" we8105desk
And the most common source IP was 192.168.250.100.

Amongst the Suricata signatures that detected the Cerber malware, which one alerted the fewest number of times? Submit ONLY the signature ID value as the answer.
I searched the Suricata sourcetype for "Ceber":
index="botsv1" "Cerber" sourcetype=suricata
And then looked to the left to find alert.signatureid and found one that only went off once: 2816763.

What fully qualified domain name (FQDN) does the Cerber ransomware attempt to direct the user to at the end of its encryption phase?
The only external IP (not starting with 192.168) as a destination is 85.93.0.0. Adding that to the search and sorting by DNS:
index="botsv1" 85.93.0.0 source="stream:dns"
That reveals: ns1.guardomicro.com
But that is not the correct answer. I then tried to sort on the souce IP of our infected computer, and rule out ARPA, the company itself, and Microsoft:
index="botsv1" sourcetype="stream:dns" src_ip=192.168.250.100 NOT arpa NOT waynecorpinc NOT microsoft | stats count by query
And that reveals: cerberhhyed5frqa.xmfir0.win

What was the first suspicious domain visited by we8105desk on 24AUG2016?
Putting that information from before into a neater-to-read table:
index="botsv1" sourcetype="stream:dns" src_ip=192.168.250.100 NOT arpa NOT waynecorpinc NOT microsoft | table _time,query
And scrolling for a bit reveals: solidaritedeproximite.org

